//! Explicit operations on foreign values the program already possesses: a raw
//! foreign reference or a provider facade presenting a foreign target. Each
//! operation acts on the underlying foreign target, under the provider,
//! session, and generation already associated with it.
//!
//! Importing this module creates no provider session or Context, performs no
//! discovery or acquisition, and confers no authority. None of its operations
//! changes ordinary Protos lookup, member read, assignment, `call`, `at`,
//! `atPut`, `each`, identity, equality, or hashing of foreign values.
//!
//! Arguments and written values cross into the foreign operation only when
//! they project losslessly; a Closure crosses only as a synchronous callback
//! scoped to that one operation. Normal results are admitted as for ordinary
//! foreign access. A failure detected before the foreign operation is entered
//! (a value that is not foreign, wrong arity, a `name` that is not a String, an
//! operation the target does not support, an argument that cannot be projected,
//! or a closed session) signals an ordinary Error. A failure after entry
//! signals a fresh `ForeignError`.

/// Explicitly executes the foreign target of `target` with `arguments` and
/// answers its admitted result. This is foreign execution, not ordinary
/// `call`: it applies even when the target is also instantiable.
invoke: ((facility) => (target, ...arguments) => {
    facility.invoke(target, ...arguments)
})(_interopFacility)

/// Explicitly instantiates the foreign target of `target` with `arguments`
/// and answers its admitted result. This is distinct from `invoke`; it applies
/// even when the target is also executable.
instantiate: ((facility) => (target, ...arguments) => {
    facility.instantiate(target, ...arguments)
})(_interopFacility)

/// Answers the admitted value of the foreign member `name`, which must be a
/// String, of the foreign target of `target`. Ordinary Protos precedence is
/// bypassed for this operation only, so foreign members such as `call`, `at`,
/// `each`, `==`, or `hash` are reachable; `target.name` is unchanged.
readMember: ((facility) => (target, name) => {
    facility.readMember(target, name)
})(_interopFacility)

/// Sets the foreign member `name`, which must be a String, of the foreign
/// target of `target` to `value` and answers exactly `value`. Nothing is read
/// back. Ordinary assignment `target.name = value` never writes a foreign
/// member.
writeMember: ((facility) => (target, name, value) => {
    facility.writeMember(target, name, value)
})(_interopFacility)

// The runtime-provisioned facility is captured privately above; it is not
// module surface.
context.removeSlot("_interopFacility")
